===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|doune}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dūn}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*dūnā|*dūn|t=sandhill, dune}}, of {{unc|en|title=uncertain origin}}. Perhaps from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*dūnaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*dūnǭ|t=pile, heap}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-|t=smoke, haze, dust}}. Alternatively, perhaps borrowed from {{der|en|cel-pro|*dūnom||hill; hillfort}} (compare {{cog|cy|din||hill}}, {{cog|ga|dún||hill, fort}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-||to finish, come full circle}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|dún||dune, sandhill}}, {{cog|nl|duin||dune, sandhill}}, {{cog|de|Düne||dune}}. More at {{m|en|town}}; akin to {{m|en|dune}}.  {{doublet|en|Down}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

